import Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.Deriv.Slope

/-!
# The Lie algebra of an arbitrary subgroup

For a subgroup `K` of a Lie group `G`, closed or not, let
`𝔨 = {X : 𝔤 | ∀ t : ℝ, lieExp (t • X) ∈ K}` be the set of derivations whose one-parameter subgroup
lies in `K`. `TauCeti.Lie.lieSubalgebraOfSubgroup K` is the Lie subalgebra generated by `𝔨`, and
for a closed `K` the generation adds nothing (`TauCeti.Lie.mem_lieSubalgebraOfSubgroup`). This
file proves that it adds nothing for every subgroup `K` of a second-countable `G`
(`TauCeti.Lie.mem_lieSubalgebraOfSubgroup_iff`): `𝔨` is itself a Lie subalgebra.

The proof has two steps.

* **The linear span of `𝔨` is a Lie subalgebra**, for every subgroup and with no countability
  hypothesis (`TauCeti.Lie.lieSubalgebraOfSubgroup_toSubmodule`). For `X, Y ∈ 𝔨` the adjoint orbit
  `s ↦ Ad (lieExp (s • X)) Y` runs inside `𝔨` and has derivative `⁅X, Y⁆` at `0`; its difference
  quotients lie in the span, which is closed, being finite-dimensional. The bracket is bilinear, so
  the span is closed under it.
* **The integral leaf subgroup of `S = Lie(K)` lies in `K`**
  (`TauCeti.Lie.integralLeafSubgroup_lieSubalgebraOfSubgroup_le`). Present the leaf as a connected
  Lie group `L` with an injective immersive homomorphism `L → G` whose differential maps `Lie(L)`
  isomorphically onto `S`. The derivations of `L` whose image lies in `𝔨` span `Lie(L)`, since `𝔨`
  spans `S`, so their one-parameter subgroups generate `L`
  (`TauCeti.closure_iUnion_range_lieExp_smul_eq_top`). Each of those one-parameter subgroups is
  carried into `K`, hence so is all of `L`.

For `X ∈ S` the one-parameter subgroup of `X` lies in the integral leaf subgroup of `S`, hence in
`K`, which is the theorem. The integral leaf subgroup is used only for its Lie group structure,
which is where second countability of `G` enters.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.Lie.lieSubalgebraOfSubgroup_toSubmodule`: the Lie algebra of an arbitrary subgroup is
  the linear span of `𝔨`.
* `TauCeti.Lie.integralLeafSubgroup_lieSubalgebraOfSubgroup_le`: the integral leaf subgroup of the
  Lie algebra of `K` lies in `K`.
* `TauCeti.Lie.mem_lieSubalgebraOfSubgroup_iff`: for every subgroup `K`, closed or not, the Lie
  algebra of `K` is exactly `𝔨`.

## References

* K.-H. Neeb, *Towards a Lie theory of locally convex groups*, Jpn. J. Math. 1 (2006),
  Remark II.6.5(b), for finite-dimensional groups through Yamabe's theorem.
* J. Hilgert and K.-H. Neeb, *Structure and Geometry of Lie Groups*, Springer (2012),
  Section 9.1, for the Lie algebra of a subgroup.
* J. M. Lee, *Introduction to Smooth Manifolds*, 2nd ed., Springer (2013), Theorem 19.26, for the
  connected Lie subgroup of a Lie subalgebra as an integral leaf.
-/

public section

noncomputable section

